Package: cjsimPWR
Type: Package
Title: Power Analyses for Conjoint Experiments Using Simulation
Version: 0.3.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Alberto", "Stefanelli", email = "alberto.stefanelli@yale.edu", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph")),
    person("Martin", "Lukac", email = "m.b.lukac@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cph")),
    person("Andrew G.", "Timm", role = c("ctb", "cph"),
           comment = "Author of the closed-form Type S and Type M code adapted from the 'retrodesign' package"))
Description: Simulation-based power analysis for forced-choice conjoint experiments that estimate
    average marginal component effects (AMCEs) as defined by Hainmueller, Hopkins and Yamamoto (2014)
    <doi:10.1093/pan/mpt024>. Choices are simulated from a logit model calibrated so that the true
    AMCEs match requested effects within a calibration tolerance, optionally with respondent
    heterogeneity and respondent subgroups. AMCEs and differences between subgroups are estimated by
    least squares with respondent-clustered standard errors. Power, Type I error and coverage are
    reported with Monte Carlo standard errors, as are the Type S and Type M errors of Gelman and Carlin
    (2014) <doi:10.1177/1745691614551642>. Extends the simulation framework of Stefanelli and Lukac
    (2020) <doi:10.31235/osf.io/spkcy>.
